{"items":[{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#5459b8f7-3fd6-4a2c-8ba9-12b59d07ff04","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"5459b8f7-3fd6-4a2c-8ba9-12b59d07ff04","dateCreated":"2026-10-02T17:27:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-10-05T23:37:25+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN now supports device posture assessment, allowing you to verify that connecting user devices meet your security and compliance requirements before granting network access. This feature integrates with your existing device posture providers, so only trusted, compliant devices can access your AWS resources through Client VPN.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePreviously, Client VPN authenticated users through certificates, SAML, or Active Directory. With device posture assessment, you can now also integrate \u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.crowdstrike.com/\"\u003eCrowdStrike\u0026nbsp;\u003c/a\u003e, \u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.jamf.com/\"\u003eJamf\u0026nbsp;\u003c/a\u003e, or \u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://jumpcloud.com/\"\u003eJumpCloud\u0026nbsp;\u003c/a\u003e with Client VPN to automatically evaluate device security signals such as compliance scores, encryption status, and risk level before allowing a connection. You define these requirements using \u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://cedarpolicy.com/\"\u003eCedar policies\u0026nbsp;\u003c/a\u003e, giving you fine-grained control over which devices can connect. To help you author and validate these policies, Client VPN provides you a Test Policy tool that guides you through creating Cedar policies for your device posture requirements.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis feature continuously re-evaluates device compliance during active sessions, and automatically disconnects a session if a device falls out of compliance, such as when risk score or security settings change. You can also use this feature in monitoring-only mode, which logs posture evaluation results without disconnecting sessions, so you can assess the impact of your policies before enforcing them. Device posture assessment works alongside your existing authorization rules to provide defense in depth.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis feature is available in all AWS Regions where AWS Client VPN is available, at no additional cost. This feature requires AWS VPN Client version 6.2.0 or later.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Client VPN:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVisit the AWS Client VPN \u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/client-vpn/\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDownload the \u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/client-vpn-download/\"\u003eAWS VPN Client\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/what-is.html\"\u003eadministrator guide\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-user/client-vpn-user-what-is.html\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2026/10/aws-client-vpn-device-posture/","postDateTime":"2026-10-05T17:00:00Z","headline":"AWS Client VPN now supports device posture assessment"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-kwf9grlgsy6veus6mx5csb-1","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-kwf9grlgsy6veus6mx5csb-1","dateCreated":"2026-09-16T18:01:53+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-09-16T18:19:44+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN now supports MacOS 27 Golden Gate client with versions 6.0+ You can now run the AWS supplied VPN client on the latest MacOS versions. AWS Client VPN desktop clients are available free of charge, and can be downloaded \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/client-vpn-download/\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nAWS Client VPN is a managed service that securely connects your remote workforce to AWS or on-premises networks. It supports desktop clients for MacOS, Windows x64, Windows Arm64 and Ubuntu-Linux. With client version 6.0 onwards, Client VPN now supports the latest MacOS\u0026nbsp; Golden Gate 27.0. It already supports Mac OS version 13.0, 14.0, 15.0, and 26.0, Windows 10 (x64) and Windows 11 (Arm64 and x64), and Ubuntu Linux 22.04 and 24.04 LTS versions.\u003cbr\u003e\nTo learn more about Client VPN:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVisit the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/what-is.html\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-user/client-vpn-user-what-is.html\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2026/09/aws-client-vpn-macos-golden-gate/","postDateTime":"2026-09-16T17:56:00Z","headline":"AWS Client VPN is now supporting MacOS 27 Golden Gate"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-kaen4qdpcjwpnmwxyygj8c","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-kaen4qdpcjwpnmwxyygj8c","dateCreated":"2026-08-13T20:49:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-08-13T21:10:16+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","nosnippet":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN introduces a rebuilt AWS VPN Client v6.0.x which offers new features like command-line interface (CLI) support, enterprise administrative controls, and faster connection establishment time, making it easier you to automate VPN connectivity and centralize device management across your organization.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nThe AWS VPN Client CLI provides full feature parity with the GUI. You can now script VPN connections into your automation workflows and infrastructure-as-code deployments. Previously, integrating VPN connectivity into automated environments required third-party tooling or manual intervention. This feature eliminates that by supporting background CLI operations. Previously, you had to distribute VPN profiles among all users in your organization, which could be managed by any user without permissions. Now, with administration controls on AWS client, you can centralize VPN policy enforcement by scoping profiles to specific users, manage global profiles available to all users on a device, and enforce approved VPN configurations across your organization.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nThe client is rebuilt with OpenVPN3, delivering faster connection establishment across all supported operating systems. You can use both the GUI and CLI together as both run concurrently and VPN connections persist independently of either interface. The rebuilt client v6.0 onwards maintains full backward compatibility with existing AWS Client VPN endpoints, so no endpoint changes are required. The updated AWS VPN Client is available today for Windows (x64/ARM), macOS (x64/ARM), and Linux (x64). There are no additional charges beyond standard pricing of AWS Client VPN.\u0026nbsp;Download the latest client version 6.0.x for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-user/client-vpn-connect-macos-release-notes.html\"\u003emacOS\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-user/client-vpn-connect-windows-release-notes.html\"\u003eWindows\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-user/client-vpn-connect-linux-release-notes.html\"\u003eLinux\u003c/a\u003e to start using it.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nTo learn more about Client VPN, visit the AWS Client VPN product page or read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-user/connect-aws-client-vpn-connect.html#cli-commands\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2026/08/aws-client-vpn-cli/","postDateTime":"2026-08-13T20:49:00Z","headline":"AWS Client VPN now supports CLI, administration controls, and faster connections"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-phpumqk6lvnr77hpped8rg","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-phpumqk6lvnr77hpped8rg","dateCreated":"2026-07-09T17:09:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-07-09T17:26:18+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN is now available in four new regions: Canada West (Calgary), Mexico (Central) and two in Asia Pacific - New Zealand and Taipei. This fully managed service enables customers to securely connect their remote workforce to resources in AWS or on-premises networks.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN eliminates the need for hardware VPN appliances and complex operational management through its pay-as-you-go model. Organizations can easily manage and monitor VPN connections through a single console.\u003cbr\u003e\nTo learn more about Client VPN:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVisit the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/pricing/\"\u003epricing page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2026/07/aws-client-vpn-four-additional-regions/","postDateTime":"2026-07-09T17:08:00Z","headline":" AWS Client VPN extends availability to four additional AWS Regions"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-ffthmtyzfdjqebtalk2p4s","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-ffthmtyzfdjqebtalk2p4s","dateCreated":"2026-05-08T22:40:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-05-08T23:05:54+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN now supports Linux desktop client with Ubuntu versions 26.04 LTS. You can now run the AWS supplied VPN client on the latest Ubuntu OS versions. AWS Client VPN desktop clients are available free of charge, and can be downloaded\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/client-vpn-download/\"\u003e here.\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nAWS Client VPN is a managed service that securely connects your remote workforce to AWS or on-premises networks. It supports desktop clients for MacOS, Windows, and Ubuntu-Linux. With this release, CVPN now supports the latest version of Ubuntu client - 26.04 LTS, along with 22.04 and 24.04. It already support Mac OS version Sonoma 14.0,, Sequoia 15.0, and Tahoe 26.0, and Windows 11. Client also supports ARM64 for MacOS and Windows.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis client version is available in all regions where AWS Client VPN is generally available with no additional cost.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nTo learn more about Client VPN:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVisit the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/what-is.html\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2026/05/aws-client-vpn-ubuntu-26/","postDateTime":"2026-05-08T22:39:00Z","headline":"AWS Client VPN now supports Ubuntu OS version 26.04 LTS "}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-w3r3xlmgyitelkwytry5g8","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-w3r3xlmgyitelkwytry5g8","dateCreated":"2026-04-23T21:15:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-04-24T16:20:18+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN now supports native integration with AWS Transit Gateway, simplifying centralized remote access for your end users across multiple VPCs and on-premises, and providing end-to-end source IP visibility.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nAWS Transit Gateway interconnects your Amazon Virtual Private Clouds (VPCs) and on-premises networks, while AWS Client VPN enables secure remote access to AWS and on-premises resources connected through your AWS network. Previously, connecting Client VPN to multiple VPCs required provisioning and managing an intermediate VPC, adding operational complexity as you needed to manage additional resources. Moreover, client source IPs were translated through Source Network Address Translation (SNAT), making it difficult to identify which remote user generated specific traffic and complicating security audits. Native Transit Gateway attachment eliminates the need for an intermediate VPC, letting you provide centralized remote access to multiple VPCs and on-premises networks directly from your Client VPN endpoint. Additionally, the end-user source IP is now preserved end-to-end, so you can create authorization rules based on actual client IPs and trace traffic back to specific users, simplifying security, compliance, and troubleshooting workflows. Furthermore, Transit Gateway flow logs capture connection-level details tied to preserved source IPs for improved troubleshooting and compliance audits.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nThis integration is available in all AWS Regions where AWS Client VPN is available. There are no additional charges for this native integration beyond standard \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/pricing/\"\u003epricing \u003c/a\u003eof AWS Client VPN and AWS Transit Gateway.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Client VPN:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVisit the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/cvpn-tgw.html\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2026/04/aws-client-vpn-transit-gateway/","postDateTime":"2026-04-23T21:11:00Z","headline":"AWS Client VPN now supports native AWS Transit Gateway integration"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-transit-gateway","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-transit-gateway","description":"general:products/aws-transit-gateway","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-pj535ptidpm3jcgngngxq1","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-pj535ptidpm3jcgngngxq1","dateCreated":"2026-01-07T20:45:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-01-07T23:00:12+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS announces a simplified onboarding experience for AWS Client VPN, introducing a new Quickstart setup method that streamlines the process of creating and configuring Client VPN endpoints.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nAWS Client VPN allows you to securely connect remote users to AWS resources and on-premises networks. The new Quickstart setup, reduces the number of steps required to set up an Client VPN endpoint. You can now easily set up Client VPN endpoints with pre-defined default configurations, requiring only three key inputs: IPv4 CIDR, server certificate ARN, and subnet selection. For example, development teams in large organizations who use Client VPN for remote access to their VPC resources for quick testing can now create endpoints quickly with the new simplified setup process.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nThe Quickstart method is available alongside the existing Standard Setup option, giving you the flexibility to choose the approach that best fits your deployment needs. Additionally, when you create a VPC, the Client VPN Quickstart workflow is automatically suggested as a follow up step. Once endpoint creation is complete, you can immediately download the client configuration file to connect using your VPN client. You can later modify and enhance your endpoint configuration using the Client VPN standard console or API as your usage patterns evolve. This enhancement is available at no additional cost in all AWS Regions where AWS Client VPN is generally available.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nTo learn more about Client VPN:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVisit the AWS Client VPN\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/what-is.html\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2026/01/aws-client-vpn-onboarding-quickstart-setup","postDateTime":"2026-01-07T20:44:00Z","headline":"AWS simplifies Client VPN onboarding with Quickstart setup"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-m78x5jqxp55ylqtwhcwguo","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-m78x5jqxp55ylqtwhcwguo","dateCreated":"2025-10-10T18:45:51+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-10-17T17:06:19+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN now supports MacOS Tahoe client with version 5.3.1. You can now run the AWS supplied VPN client on the latest MacOS versions. AWS Client VPN desktop clients are available free of charge, and can be downloaded \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/client-vpn-download/\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nAWS Client VPN is a managed service that securely connects your remote workforce to AWS or on-premises networks. It supports desktop clients for MacOS, Windows x64, Windows Arm64 and Ubuntu-Linux. With client version 5.3.1 onwards, Client VPN now supports the MacOS Tahoe 26.0. It already supports Mac OS version 13.0, 14.0 and 15.0, Windows 10 (x64) and Windows 11 (Arm64 and x64), and Ubuntu Linux 22.04 and 24.04 LTS versions.\u003cbr\u003e\nTo learn more about Client VPN:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVisit the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/what-is.html\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-user/client-vpn-user-what-is.html\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/10/aws-client-vpn-macos-tahoe/","postDateTime":"2025-10-10T18:44:00Z","headline":"AWS Client VPN is now supporting MacOS Tahoe"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-kwf9grlgsy6veus6mx5csb","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-kwf9grlgsy6veus6mx5csb","dateCreated":"2025-08-27T19:46:32+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-09-03T22:08:46+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN now supports Windows Arm64 client with version 5.3.0. You can now run the AWS supplied VPN client on the latest Windows Arm64 OS versions. AWS Client VPN desktop clients are available free of charge, and can be downloaded \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/client-vpn-download/\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nAWS Client VPN is a managed service that securely connects your remote workforce to AWS or on-premises networks. It supports desktop clients for MacOS, Windows x64, Windows Arm64 and Ubuntu-Linux. With this release, Client VPN now supports the Windows Arm64 5.3.0. It already supports Mac OS version 13.0, 14.0 and 15.0, Windows 10 (x64) and Windows 11 (Arm64 and x64), and Ubuntu Linux 22.04 and 24.04 LTS versions.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nThis client version is available in all regions where AWS Client VPN is generally available with no additional cost.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nTo learn more about Client VPN:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVisit the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/what-is.html\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-user/client-vpn-user-what-is.html\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/08/aws-client-vpn-windows-arm64/","postDateTime":"2025-08-27T19:43:00Z","headline":"AWS Client VPN extends OS support to Windows Arm64 v5.3.0"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-jfwvqvodebcmusxbmnrn72","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-jfwvqvodebcmusxbmnrn72","dateCreated":"2025-08-26T22:00:53+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-09-03T22:09:42+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS Client VPN announces support for remote access to IPv6 workloads, allowing customers to establish secure VPN connections to their IPv6-enabled VPC resources. This new capability enables customers to meet their compliance and IPv6 network adoption goals. Now organizations can support IPv4, IPv6, and dual-stack resource connectivity through their Client VPN endpoints.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nPreviously, Client VPN only supported remote access to IPv4-enabled AWS workloads. With this feature, administrators can now support IPv6-enabled resources using IPv6-only or dual-stack Client VPN endpoints. Organizations can now directly connect their remote users to IPv6 resources and maintain end-to-end IPv6-only connectivity. For example, organizations can now use IPv6-enabled devices to remotely access IPv6-enabled resources in VPC via Client VPN, preserving end-to-end IPv6 connectivity. This feature simplifies network architecture for organizations using IPv6 while preserving native protocol preferences.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nThis feature is available in all regions where AWS Client VPN is generally available, except the Middle East (Bahrain) Region, and comes with no additional cost. Customers can use IPv6 and dual-stack endpoints at the current endpoint per-hour price.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nTo learn more about Client VPN:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVisit the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/what-is.html\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-user/client-vpn-user-what-is.html\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/08/aws-client-vpn-connectivity-ipv6-resources","postDateTime":"2025-08-26T21:12:00Z","headline":"AWS Client VPN now supports connectivity to IPv6 resources"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#p229557904","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-uq5gbJKgvUDPUVHqn7M6SQ","dateCreated":"2025-04-25T18:54:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-04-28T17:25:44+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS announced a new AWS Client VPN feature that monitors device networking routes, prevents VPN traffic leaks, and strengthens remote access security. The feature continuously tracks your users\u0026#39; device routing tables to ensure outbound traffic flows through the VPN tunnel according to your configured settings. If the feature detects any modified networking route settings, it automatically restores the routes to your original configuration.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nAWS Client VPN allows admins to configure routes on users\u0026#39; devices to route traffic through the VPN. For example, an admin might configure end users\u0026#39; devices to connect to the 10.0.0.0/24 network using VPN connectivity while the rest of the traffic breaks out locally from the device. However, connected devices could deviate from the organization\u0026#39;s configurations, causing VPN leaks. For example, even if you configure traffic to the 10.0.0.0/24 network to go via VPN, users or other clients running on the device can modify settings and bypass VPN for this traffic. With this feature enabled, our VPN client will continuously monitor routes and automatically correct deviations by repairing routes back to the original configuration. This feature ensures admin\u0026#39;s configuration is consistently applied to end users, maintaining the connection integrity of your organization.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nThis feature is available in all regions where AWS Client VPN is generally available with no additional cost.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nTo learn more about Client VPN:\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cul\u003e\n\t\u003cli\u003eVisit the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\t\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN Client Route Enforcement \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/cvpn-working-cre.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/04/aws-client-vpn-client-routes-enforcement/","postDateTime":"2025-04-28T10:00:00-07:00","headline":"AWS Client VPN now supports Client Routes Enforcement"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#p207498524","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"1YqqZLUZWn66WRr9tBCYXM","dateCreated":"2025-03-17T18:21:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-03-18T17:03:44+0000","additionalFields":{"headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/03/aws-client-vpn-authorization-rules-route-quotas","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS announces increased quotas for AWS Client VPN, expanding routes per target network association to 100 and authorization rules per endpoint to 200.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nAWS Client VPN allows you to securely manage network routing and access control for your VPN connections. Previously, you were given default quota of 10 routes per association and 50 authorization rules per endpoint. With this quota increase, you can now configure up to 100 routes per association and 200 rules per endpoint. For example, enterprises with distributed architectures can define specific routing paths for multiple subnets across development, staging, and production environments, providing greater flexibility and granular control over network traffic flows.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nThese new quotas are default configurations and can be adjusted to a higher limit as well. These default quotas are automatically applied to all new and existing Client VPN endpoints. This enhancement is available at no additional cost in all AWS Regions where AWS Client VPN is generally available.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nTo learn more about Client VPN:\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cul\u003e\n\t\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/limits.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003equotas page\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\t\u003cli\u003eVisit the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\t\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n","postDateTime":"2025-03-18T13:00:00-04:00","headline":"AWS Client VPN increases authorization rules and route quotas "}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#p186036050","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-6KFJkkWyAjzzsuvw2Lv6j6","dateCreated":"2025-01-21T19:15:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-01-22T22:53:33+0000","additionalFields":{"headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/01/aws-client-vpn-concurrent-vpn-connections/","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS announces the general availability of concurrent VPN connections for AWS Client VPN. This feature allows you to securely connect to multiple Client VPN connections simultaneously, enabling access to your resources across different work environments.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nAWS Client VPN allows your users to securely connect to your network remotely from any location. Previously, you could only connect to one VPN profile at a time. This limited your access to only one network. To access another network, you were required to disconnect and reconnect to a different VPN profile. With this launch, you can connect to multiple VPN profiles simultaneously without switching. For example, software developers using AWS client for VPN can now connect to development, test, and production environment concurrently. This feature allows seamless parallel connections to all required environments, significantly improving productivity for end users.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nThis feature is available only with AWS-supplied Client VPN client version 5.0+. You can download this version following the steps \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/client-vpn-download/\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e. This feature and the required client version are available at no additional cost in all AWS regions where AWS Client VPN is generally available.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nTo learn more about Client VPN:\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cul\u003e\n\t\u003cli\u003eVisit the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\t\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n","postDateTime":"2025-01-22T10:00:00-08:00","headline":"AWS Client VPN announces support for concurrent VPN connections"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#p165617382","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-uW1ffWjnSYruG3VV75hRen","dateCreated":"2024-11-12T19:58:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-11-13T18:06:43+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN now supports Linux desktop client with Ubuntu versions 22.04 LTS and 24.04 LTS. You can now run the AWS supplied VPN client on the latest Ubuntu OS versions. AWS Client VPN desktop clients are available free of charge, and can be downloaded \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/client-vpn-download/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nAWS Client VPN is a managed service that securely connects your remote workforce to AWS or on-premises networks. It supports desktop clients for MacOS, Windows, and Ubuntu-Linux. With this release, CVPN now supports the latest version of Ubuntu client (i.e. 22.04 LTS and 24.04 LTS). It already support Mac OS version 12.0, 13.0 and 14.0, and Windows 10 and 11.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nThis client version is available in all regions where AWS Client VPN is generally available with no additional cost.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nTo learn more about Client VPN:\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cul\u003e\n\t\u003cli\u003eVisit the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\t\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/11/aws-client-vpn-supports-latest-ubuntu-os-versions/","postDateTime":"2024-11-13T10:00:00-08:00","headline":"AWS Client VPN now supports the latest Ubuntu OS versions - 22.04 LTS and 24.04 LTS"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-09-17T18:03:36+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-11-aws-client-vpn-additional-aws-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/11/aws-client-vpn-additional-aws-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-14T19:20:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:00:29+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can use AWS Client VPN in four additional AWS (UAE, Melbourne, Spain, and Zurich) Regions. Using AWS Client VPN customers can provide secure access to their resources in AWS or on-premises network for their remote workforce. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith AWS Client VPN, organizations can now provide highly available and secure VPN access to all their employees regardless of their location. AWS Client VPN is a pay-as-you-go, fully managed service that eliminates the capital expense of buying hardware VPN appliances and the operational complexity of scaling and patching. Customers can choose certificate-based, Active Directory, or SAML based authentication, and benefit from tighter security controls by defining access control rules based on groups. All this is done using a single console, where customers can easily monitor and manage their AWS Client VPN connections.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN allows customers to choose from AWS VPN Desktop Client or OpenVPN-based clients, giving their employees the option to use the device of their choice.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Client VPN:\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eVisit the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\r\nRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-11-14T19:07:43Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/11/aws-client-vpn-additional-aws-regions/","postDateTime":"2023-11-14T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Client VPN extends availability to four additional AWS Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can use AWS Client VPN in four additional AWS (UAE, Melbourne, Spain, and Zurich) Regions. Using AWS Client VPN customers can provide secure access to their resources in AWS or on-premises network for their remote workforce. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-10-aws-client-vpn-additional-aws-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/10/aws-client-vpn-additional-aws-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:06:31+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:58:10+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can use AWS Client VPN in three additional Asia Pacific (Osaka, Hyderabad, and Jakarta) Regions. Using AWS Client VPN customers can provide secure access to their resources in AWS or on-premises network for their remote workforce.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith AWS Client VPN, organizations can now provide highly available and secure VPN access to all their employees regardless of their location. AWS Client VPN is a pay-as-you-go, fully managed service that eliminates the capital expense of buying hardware VPN appliances and the operational complexity of scaling and patching. Customers can choose certificate-based, Active Directory, or SAML based authentication, and benefit from tighter security controls by defining access control rules based on groups. All this is done using a single console, where customers can easily monitor and manage their AWS Client VPN connections.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN allows customers to choose from AWS VPN Desktop Client or OpenVPN-based clients, giving their employees the option to use the device of their choice.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Client VPN:\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003eVisit the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-10-30T14:09:08Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/10/aws-client-vpn-additional-aws-regions/","postDateTime":"2023-10-16T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Client VPN extends availability to three additional AWS Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can use AWS Client VPN in three additional Asia Pacific (Osaka, Hyderabad, and Jakarta) Regions. Using AWS Client VPN customers can provide secure access to their resources in AWS or on-premises network for their remote workforce.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-08-aws-client-vpn-israel-tel-aviv-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/aws-client-vpn-israel-tel-aviv-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:01:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:35:15+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can use AWS Client VPN in Israel (Tel Aviv) Region. You can now provide VPN access to your remote workforce to securely access resources in the Israel (Tel Aviv) Region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN provides highly available and secure VPN access to all of your employees, regardless of their location. AWS Client VPN is a pay-as-you-go, fully managed service that eliminates the capital expense of buying hardware VPN appliances and the operational complexity of scaling and patching. Choose certificate-based, Active Directory, or SAML based authentication, and benefit from tighter security controls by defining access control rules based on groups. All this is done using a single console, where you easily monitor and manage your AWS Client VPN connections.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN allows you to choose from AWS VPN Desktop Client or OpenVPN-based clients, giving your employees the option to use the device of their choice.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Client VPN:\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003eVisit the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-09-01T13:08:07Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/aws-client-vpn-israel-tel-aviv-region/","postDateTime":"2023-08-17T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Client VPN now supports Israel (Tel Aviv) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can use AWS Client VPN in Israel (Tel Aviv) Region. You can now provide VPN access to your remote workforce to securely access resources in the Israel (Tel Aviv) Region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-01-aws-vpn-banner-text-maximum-session-duration","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/01/aws-vpn-banner-text-maximum-session-duration/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:34:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:18:50+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN now provides the ability for all customers to display a customizable banner on the AWS Client VPN Desktop application when a VPN session is established. The banner text can contain privacy and security notices that will be displayed to end-users before granting VPN access. Customers will now be able to configure the banner text using the AWS Console or API, and be displayed on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-user/release-notes.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Client Desktop applications\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;(AWS Client VPN for Windows v2.0.0 or higher, AWS Client VPN for MacOS v2.0.0 or higher,  AWS Client VPN for Ubuntu Linux v2.0.0 or higher). Customers will also be able to configure the maximum session duration to can help them meet certain security and compliance requirements. The maximum session duration is a trigger by which end-users are required to re-authenticate prior to establishing a VPN session. \u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN administrators can configure these features using the AWS Console or AWS CLI and is available in all AWS Client VPN commercial and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/govcloud-us/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US)\u003c/a\u003e regions. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN helps provide highly available and secure VPN access for organizations, regardless of their location. AWS Client VPN is a pay-as-you-go managed service, that helps eliminate the need to deal with the capital expense of buying hardware VPN appliances, or the operational complexity of scaling and patching such appliances. Customers can choose certificate-based, Active Directory, or SAML based authentication, and benefit from tighter security controls by defining access control rules based on groups. Using a single console, you can easily monitor and manage all of your VPN connections. AWS Client VPN allows you to choose from AWS VPN Desktop Clients or OpenVPN-based clients giving your employees the option to use the device of their choice to connect.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Client VPN:\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003eVisit the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-01-20T21:58:55Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/01/aws-vpn-banner-text-maximum-session-duration/","postDateTime":"2022-01-20T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Client VPN now supports banner text and maximum session duration","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN now provides the ability for all customers to display a customizable banner on the AWS Client VPN Desktop application when a VPN session is established. The banner text can contain privacy and security notices that will be displayed to end-users before granting VPN access. Customers will now be able to configure the banner text using the AWS Console or API, and be displayed on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-user/release-notes.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Client Desktop applications\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;(AWS Client VPN for Windows v2.0.0 or higher, AWS Client VPN for MacOS v2.0.0 or higher,  AWS Client VPN for Ubuntu Linux v2.0.0 or higher). Customers will also be able to configure the maximum session duration to can help them meet certain security and compliance requirements. The maximum session duration is a trigger by which end-users are required to re-authenticate prior to establishing a VPN session. \u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-06-aws-client-vpn-launches-desktop-client-for-linux","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/06/aws-client-vpn-launches-desktop-client-for-linux/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:46:21+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:08:48+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN now supports SAML based federated authentication for opening a VPN connection from a Linux Desktop Operating system (Ubuntu 64bit 18.04 and 20.04 LTS).  The Linux Desktop client has feature parity with the existing Windows and macOS Desktop clients. AWS Client VPN Desktop Clients are available free of charge, and can be downloaded \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/client-vpn-download/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.  \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN helps you provide highly available and secure VPN access to all of your employees, regardless of their location. AWS Client VPN is a pay-as-you-go fully-managed service, eliminating the need to deal with the capital expense of buying hardware VPN appliances, or the operational complexity of scaling and patching. Customers can choose certificate-based, Active Directory, or SAML based authentication, and benefit from tighter security controls by defining access control rules based on groups. Using a single console, you monitor and manage all of your VPN connections. AWS Client VPN allows you to choose from AWS VPN Desktop Client or OpenVPN-based clients, giving your employees the option to use the device of their choice, including Windows, Mac, iOS, Android and Linux.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN allows you to choose from AWS VPN Desktop Client or OpenVPN-based clients, giving your employees the option to use the device of their choice.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Client VPN:\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan\u003eVisit the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-06-23T19:39:00Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/06/aws-client-vpn-launches-desktop-client-for-linux/","postDateTime":"2021-06-23T11:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Client VPN launches desktop client for Linux","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN now supports SAML based federated authentication for opening a VPN connection from a Linux Desktop Operating system (Ubuntu 64bit 18.04 and 20.04 LTS).  The Linux Desktop client has feature parity with the existing Windows and macOS Desktop clients. AWS Client VPN Desktop Clients are available free of charge, and can be downloaded \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/vpn/client-vpn-download.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.  \u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:28+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:28+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-06-aws-client-vpn-launches-in-aws-govcloud-us-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/06/aws-client-vpn-launches-in-aws-govcloud-us-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:45:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:08:30+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN is now available in\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/govcloud-us/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US)\u003c/a\u003e. You can now provide VPN access to your remote workforce to securely access resources in AWS GovCloud (US) regions.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN provides highly available and secure VPN access to all of your employees, regardless of their location. AWS Client VPN is a pay-as-you-go fully-managed service, eliminating the need to deal with the capital expense of buying hardware VPN appliances, or the operational complexity of scaling and patching. Customers can choose certificate-based, Active Directory, or SAML based authentication, and benefit from tighter security controls by defining access control rules based on groups. Using a single console, you easily monitor and manage all of your VPN connections. AWS Client VPN allows you to choose from AWS VPN Desktop Client or OpenVPN-based clients, giving your employees the option to use the device of their choice, including Windows, Mac, iOS, Android and Linux.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN allows you to choose from AWS VPN Desktop Client or OpenVPN-based clients, giving your employees the option to use the device of their choice.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Client VPN:\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003eVisit the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-06-11T21:12:38Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/06/aws-client-vpn-launches-in-aws-govcloud-us-regions/","postDateTime":"2021-06-11T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Client VPN launches in AWS GovCloud (US) Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN is now available in\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/govcloud-us.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US)\u003c/a\u003e. You can now provide VPN access to your remote workforce to securely access resources in AWS GovCloud (US) regions.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-03-aws-client-vpn-announces-expanded-presence-inside-six-aws-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/03/aws-client-vpn-announces-expanded-presence-inside-six-aws-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:43:32+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:04:54+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN has expanded the number of Availability Zones supported inside the US East (Northern Virginia), US West (Oregon), Asia Pacific (Mumbai), Asia Pacific (Seoul), Asia Pacific (Sydney), and Canada (Central) regions.  This expansion gives you more zones to choose from and additional flexibility when associating subnets. This change also increases the number of concurrent connections you can make per endpoint in these Regions.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN enables you to provide highly available and secure VPN access to all of your employees, regardless of their location. As AWS Client VPN is a cloud solution, you don’t need to install and manage hardware or software-based solutions, or try to estimate how many remote users you need to support at any one time. You can choose certificate-based, Active Directory, or SAML based authentication, and benefit from tighter security controls by defining access control rules based on groups. Using a single console, you can easily monitor and manage all of your VPN connections. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN allows you to choose from AWS VPN Desktop Client or OpenVPN-based clients, giving your employees the option to use the device of their choice.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, see the AWS VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e, as well as the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/what-is.html\"\u003eadministrator\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-user/user-getting-started.html\"\u003euser\u003c/a\u003e documentation.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-03-22T20:47:57Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/03/aws-client-vpn-announces-expanded-presence-inside-six-aws-regions/","postDateTime":"2021-03-22T17:12:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Client VPN announces expanded presence inside six AWS Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN has expanded the number of Availability Zones supported inside the US East (Northern Virginia), US West (Oregon), Asia Pacific (Mumbai), Asia Pacific (Seoul), Asia Pacific (Sydney), and Canada (Central) regions.  This expansion gives you more zones to choose from and additional flexibility when associating subnets. This change also increases the number of concurrent connections you can make per endpoint in these Regions.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-11-aws-client-vpn-adds-support-in-additional-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/aws-client-vpn-adds-support-in-additional-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:04:29+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:11:29+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN is now available in the Paris, Milan, Cape Town, Bahrain, and Hong Kong Regions. This increases global coverage of AWS Client VPN and brings the total number of available Regions to twenty.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN provides highly available and secure VPN access to all of your employees, regardless of their location. AWS Client VPN is a pay-as-you-go fully-managed service, eliminating the need to deal with the capital expense of buying hardware VPN appliances, or the operational complexity of scaling and patching. Customers can choose certificate-based, Active Directory, or SAML based authentication, and benefit from tighter security controls by defining access control rules based on groups. Using a single console, you easily monitor and manage all of your VPN connections. AWS Client VPN allows you to choose from AWS VPN Desktop Client or OpenVPN-based clients, giving your employees the option to use the device of their choice, including Windows, Mac, iOS, Android and Linux.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith these new Regions, AWS Client VPN is now available in the Asia Pacific (Bahrain, Hong Kong, Mumbai, Seoul, Singapore, Sydney, Tokyo), Canada (Central), EU (Frankfurt, Ireland, London, Milan, Paris, Stockholm), North America (N. Virginia, Northern California, Ohio, Oregon), Africa (Cape Town), South America (Sao Paulo). \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Client VPN:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVisit the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-11-23T17:36:56Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/aws-client-vpn-adds-support-in-additional-regions/","postDateTime":"2020-11-23T12:41:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Client VPN adds support in additional Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN is now available in the Paris, Milan, Cape Town, Bahrain, and Hong Kong Regions. This increases global coverage of AWS Client VPN and brings the total number of available Regions to twenty.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:41+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-11-aws-client-vpn-supports-client-connect-handler","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/aws-client-vpn-supports-client-connect-handler/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:06:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:10:42+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN is a managed, scalable, virtual private network service that enables users to securely access both AWS resources and on-premises networks. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now enforce additional security authorization policies on connections to a Client VPN endpoint by configuring a client connect handler (referred to as the handler in this post). The handler enables customers to run custom authorization logic during connection establishment after the Client VPN service has authenticated the devices (or users).   The handler is implemented through a AWS Lambda function, and can be enabled through the AWS Console or AWS CLI.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe handler protects customer investments by taking advantage of the existing policies defined (and enforced) in Identity Provider and Mobile Device Management (MDM) software.  The handler allows enterprise IT administrators to enforce access based on IP address, geolocation and time (for example: deny access during a maintenance window, or allow access during certain hours).     End-users in enterprise organizations might bring their own devices (BYOD), that might require additional security authorization checks and posture assessment (for example: minimum version of Operating System), which can help enforce remediation actions.   The handler can also be customized for gathering connection establishment auditing information for certain devices (or users).  \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCustomers of Client VPN can immediately take advantage of Client Connect Handler at no additional cost.  This feature is available in all regions where AWS Client VPN operates.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Client VPN:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVisit the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-11-05T20:27:05Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/aws-client-vpn-supports-client-connect-handler/","postDateTime":"2020-11-05T11:19:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Client VPN now supports Client Connect Handler ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN is a managed, scalable, virtual private network service that enables users to securely access both AWS resources and on-premises networks. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-11-aws-client-vpn-announces-self-service-portal","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/aws-client-vpn-announces-self-service-portal/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:12:32+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:14:30+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eThe Client VPN self-service portal is a read-only web portal that helps end-users of Client VPN to download VPN Profile and updated versions of AWS Client VPN desktop application. End-users will be able to download the VPN profile and desktop application directly to their computers.   We will also continue to support the ability for end-users to directly download the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/client-vpn-download/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edesktop application\u003c/a\u003e without the need to enter any credentials. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo access the self service portal, the end-user is required to enter username and password credentials for authentication through your Federated Identity provider (SAML2.0 based) or Active Directory. Your Client VPN Endpoint Administrator will send an email with detailed instructions to access the Self Service portal. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAll customers of Client VPN will be able to immediately take advantage of this feature at no additional cost and available in all regions where AWS Client VPN operates.  \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Client VPN:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVisit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Client VPN product page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRead the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Client VPN documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-11-04T18:45:27Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/aws-client-vpn-announces-self-service-portal/","postDateTime":"2020-11-04T12:51:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Client VPN announces self service portal to download VPN profiles and desktop applications","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eThe Client VPN self-service portal is a read-only web portal that helps end-users of Client VPN to download VPN Profile and updated versions of AWS Client VPN desktop application. End-users will be able to download the VPN profile and desktop application directly to their computers.   We will also continue to support the ability for end-users to directly download the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/vpn/client-vpn-download.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edesktop application\u003c/a\u003e without the need to enter any credentials. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-10-aws-client-vpn-available-sao-paulo","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/10/aws-client-vpn-available-sao-paulo/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:07:03+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:12:36+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN is now available in the South America (Sao Paulo) Region. This increases global coverage of AWS Client VPN, which offers region support in Asia Pacific (Mumbai, Seoul, Singapore, Sydney, Tokyo), Canada (Central), EU (Frankfurt, Ireland, London, Stockholm), North America (N. Virginia, Northern California, Ohio, Oregon). With this launch, AWS Client VPN is now available in a total of 15 Regions.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith AWS Client VPN, you can provide highly available and secure VPN access to all of your employees regardless of their location. AWS Client VPN is a pay-as-you-go fully-managed service, eliminating the need to deal with the capital expense of buying hardware VPN appliances, or the operational complexity of scaling and patching. Customers can choose certificate-based, Active Directory, or SAML based authentication, and benefit from tighter security controls by defining access control rules based on groups. Using a single console, you can easily monitor and manage all of your VPN connections. AWS Client VPN allows you to choose from AWS VPN Desktop Client or OpenVPN-based clients, giving your employees the option to use the device of their choice, including Windows, Mac, iOS, Android and Linux.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS VPN product page\u003c/a\u003e, as well as the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eadministrator\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-user/user-getting-started.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003euser\u003c/a\u003e documentation.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-10-07T17:29:06Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/10/aws-client-vpn-available-sao-paulo/","postDateTime":"2020-10-07T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Client VPN is now available in the South America (Sao Paulo) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN is now available in the South America (Sao Paulo) Region. This increases global coverage of AWS Client VPN, which offers region support in Asia Pacific (Mumbai, Seoul, Singapore, Sydney, Tokyo), Canada (Central), EU (Frankfurt, Ireland, London, Stockholm), North America (N. Virginia, Northern California, Ohio, Oregon). With this launch, AWS Client VPN is now available in a total of 15 Regions.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-09-aws-client-vpn-now-supports-client-to-client-connectivity","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/09/aws-client-vpn-now-supports-client-to-client-connectivity/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:06:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:16:52+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan style\u003d\"color: #16191f;\"\u003eAWS Client VPN is a managed, scalable, virtual private network service that enables users to securely access both AWS resources and on-premises networks. By enabling Client-to-Client connectivity in either the AWS Console or through the AWS CLI, a VPN client can establish a secure connection to another VPN client. \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCustomers now have the ability to create local routes between VPN clients connected to the same AWS Client VPN endpoint.  This feature will allow one VPN client to initiate a connection to another VPN client, which have established a session with the AWS VPN Client endpoint.   For example, a developer who has an active VPN connection is able to interface with on-premises resource(s) that has also has an active VPN connection(s) on the same AWS Client VPN endpoint. This allows for establishing a secure connection without changing network security policies. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAll customers of Client VPN will be able to immediately take advantage of this feature at no additional cost and available in all regions where AWS Client VPN operates.  \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Client VPN:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVisit the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRead the AWS Client VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-09-30T17:04:39Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/09/aws-client-vpn-now-supports-client-to-client-connectivity/","postDateTime":"2020-09-30T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Client VPN now supports client to client connectivity","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan style\u003d\"color: #16191f;\"\u003eAWS Client VPN is a managed, scalable, virtual private network service that enables users to securely access both AWS resources and on-premises networks. By enabling Client-to-Client connectivity in either the AWS Console or through the AWS CLI, a VPN client can establish a secure connection to another VPN client. \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-05-aws-client-vpn-supports-federated-authentication-via-saml-2","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/05/aws-client-vpn-supports-federated-authentication-via-saml-2/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:10:44+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN is a managed, scalable virtual private network service that enables users to securely access AWS resources and on-premises networks. Federated Authentication makes it easy to integrate AWS Client VPN user authentication and authorization with a centralized, SAML based Identity Provider (IdP). \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the addition of Federated Authentication, AWS Client VPN now supports three methods of authentication: Mutual authentication via client certificates, user authentication via Active Directory, and user Federated Authentication via SAML. Using Active Directory or Federated Authentication, customers can control access to associated networks by specifying authorization rules when configuring their AWS Client VPN endpoint. Active Directory group SIDs or SAML-based IdP group names can be directly referenced from each authorization rule.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFederated Authentication is now available in Americas (Montreal), Americas (N California), Americas (N Virginia), Americas (Ohio), Americas (Oregon), Asia Pacific (Mumbai), Asia Pacific (Seoul), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), EU (Ireland), EU (Frankfurt), EU (London), and EU (Stockholm). \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Federated Authentication:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRead the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/networking-and-content-delivery/authenticate-aws-client-vpn-users-with-saml/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS News blog post\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVisit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Client VPN product page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRead the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Client VPN documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-05-19T19:27:20Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/05/aws-client-vpn-supports-federated-authentication-via-saml-2/","postDateTime":"2020-05-19T12:05:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Client VPN now supports Federated Authentication via SAML 2.0","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN is a managed, scalable virtual private network service that enables users to securely access AWS resources and on-premises networks. Federated Authentication makes it easy to integrate AWS Client VPN user authentication and authorization with a centralized, SAML based Identity Provider (IdP). \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-02-introducing-the-desktop-client-for-aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/02/introducing-the-desktop-client-for-aws-client-vpn/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:01:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T12:59:40+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eWe are excited to announce AWS Client VPN for desktop, an application which runs on Mac and Windows devices and provides access to Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) and on premise networks through AWS Client VPN endpoints.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePreviously, customers needed to use third-party OpenVPN clients to access AWS Client VPN endpoints. These clients provide basic connectivity but lack advanced authentication and management capabilities.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN for Desktop is built by AWS and works seamlessly with AWS Client VPN endpoints. Customers now have an end-to-end solution designed, built, and operated by AWS. To get started with AWS Client VPN for desktop you can download the installer \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/client-vpn-download/\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e. For more information about AWS Client VPN, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\"\u003evisit\u003c/a\u003e the product page.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-02-05T22:10:58Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/02/introducing-the-desktop-client-for-aws-client-vpn/","postDateTime":"2020-02-05T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Introducing the Desktop Client for AWS Client VPN","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eWe are excited to announce AWS Client VPN for desktop, an application which runs on Mac and Windows devices and provides access to Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) and on premise networks through AWS Client VPN endpoints.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-10-aws-client-vpn-now-available-seoul-canada-central-stockholm-northern-california-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/aws-client-vpn-now-available-seoul-canada-central-stockholm-northern-california-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:07:56+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:25:09+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN is now available in Asia Pacific (Seoul), Canada (Central), EU (Stockholm), North America (Northern California) regions. The addition of these regions increases availability of AWS Client VPN, which offers region support in Asia Pacific (Mumbai, Singapore, Sydney, Tokyo), EU (Frankfurt, Ireland, London), North America (N. Virginia, Ohio, Oregon)   With this launch, AWS Client VPN is now available in a total of 14 regions.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith AWS Client VPN, you can provide highly available and secure VPN access to all of your employees regardless of their location. AWS Client VPN is a pay-as-you-go fully-managed service, eliminating the need to deal with the capital expense of buying hardware VPN appliances, or the operational complexity of scaling and patching. Customers can choose certificate-based, Active Directory, or multi factor authentication, and benefit from tighter security controls by defining access control rules based on Active Directory groups. Using a single console, you can easily monitor and manage all of your VPN connections. AWS Client VPN allows you to choose from OpenVPN-based clients, giving your employees the option to use the device of their choice, including Windows, Mac, iOS, Android and Linux.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\"\u003eAWS VPN product page\u003c/a\u003e, as well as the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/what-is.html\"\u003eadministrator\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-user/user-getting-started.html\"\u003euser documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-31T18:25:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/aws-client-vpn-now-available-seoul-canada-central-stockholm-northern-california-regions/","postDateTime":"2019-10-31T12:28:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Client VPN is now available in Asia Pacific (Seoul), Canada (Central), EU (Stockholm), North America (Northern California) regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN is now available in Asia Pacific (Seoul), Canada (Central), EU (Stockholm), North America (Northern California) regions. The addition of these regions increases availability of AWS Client VPN, which offers region support in Asia Pacific (Mumbai, Singapore, Sydney, Tokyo), EU (Frankfurt, Ireland, London), North America (N. Virginia, Ohio, Oregon)   With this launch, AWS Client VPN is now available in a total of 14 regions.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-09-aws-client-vpn-now-supports-multi-factor-authentication-for-active-directory","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/09/aws-client-vpn-now-supports-multi-factor-authentication-for-active-directory/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:10:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:15:54+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now enable Multi Factor Authentication (MFA) capabilities for your users using AWS Client VPN and Active Directory. Enterprises can now create a second layer of defense by prompting the user for additional factor, such as verifying a push notification or an email OTP.  \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can enable and use MFA with AD support for Client VPN using the AWS Directory Services console or programmatically via the AWS SDK at no additional cost. For more information on setting up MFA visit documentation provided by Directory Services, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/directoryservice/latest/admin-guide/ms_ad_mfa.html\"\u003eEnabling MFA with AD for Managed Microsoft AD\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/directoryservice/latest/admin-guide/ad_connector_mfa.html\"\u003eEnabling MFA with AD for AD Connector\u003c/a\u003e. Learn more about \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/what-is.html\"\u003eAWS Client VPN\u003c/a\u003e by visiting the provided documentation.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:02:36Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/09/aws-client-vpn-now-supports-multi-factor-authentication-for-active-directory/","postDateTime":"2019-09-30T13:34:45Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Client VPN now supports Multi Factor Authentication for Active Directory","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now enable Multi Factor Authentication (MFA) capabilities for your users using AWS Client VPN and Active Directory. Enterprises can now create a second layer of defense by prompting the user for additional factor, such as verifying a push notification or an email OTP.  \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-directory-service","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-directory-service","description":"general:products/aws-directory-service","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:28+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:28+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-06-aws-client-vpn-includes-support-for-aws-cloudformation","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/06/aws-client-vpn-includes-support-for-aws-cloudformation/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:05:34+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:22:01+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use AWS CloudFormation templates to specify AWS Client VPN Endpoint resources. This improvement enables you to use CloudFormation to create AWS Client VPN Endpoints, associate target subnets, create routes and rules —along with the rest of your AWS infrastructure—in a secure, efficient, and repeatable way. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCloudFormation support for AWS Client VPN endpoint resources is available in all of the AWS Regions where AWS Client VPN is available. AWS Client VPN is available in US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), EU (Ireland), EU (Frankfurt), EU (London), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Mumbai) and Asia Pacific (Tokyo).\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information about the list of resources supported by CloudFormation including the AWS Client VPN endpoints, refer to: \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/AWS_EC2.html\"\u003ehttps://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/AWS_EC2.html\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:01:17Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/06/aws-client-vpn-includes-support-for-aws-cloudformation/","postDateTime":"2019-06-14T10:01:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Client VPN now includes support for AWS CloudFormation","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use AWS CloudFormation templates to specify AWS Client VPN Endpoint resources. This improvement enables you to use CloudFormation to create AWS Client VPN Endpoints, associate target subnets, create routes and rules —along with the rest of your AWS infrastructure—in a secure, efficient, and repeatable way. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-cloudformation","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-cloudformation","description":"general:products/aws-cloudformation","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-05-aws-client-vpn-now-available-in-asia-pacific-mumbai-and-asia-pacific-tokyo-aws-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/05/aws-client-vpn-now-available-in-asia-pacific-mumbai-and-asia-pacific-tokyo-aws-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:11:37+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:22:11+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN is now available in the Asia Pacific (Mumbai) and Asia Pacific (Tokyo) AWS Regions. AWS Client VPN is already available in US East (Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon),\u0026nbsp;EU (Frankfurt), EU (Ireland),\u0026nbsp;EU (London),\u0026nbsp;Asia Pacific (Singapore), and Asia Pacific (Sydney) AWS Regions. Support for other AWS Regions is coming soon.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN is a managed service that provides you with the ability to securely access your AWS and on-premises networks from anywhere, using OpenVPN-based clients.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEmployees often need to access company resources while off premises, such as at home or on the road. Until today, to enable access, you could run a hardware VPN appliance in your data center or deploy a software-based VPN appliance on Amazon EC2. Setup, security, and maintenance of self-managed client-based VPN solutions present an operational challenge and ongoing burden. Unforeseen events, such as a snow day, could require a large number of employees to connect from a remote location and further strain your VPN. It often led to reduced VPN availability for employees.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith AWS Client VPN, you can now provide highly available and secure VPN access to all your employees regardless of their location. AWS Client VPN is a pay-as-you-go fully-managed service, eliminating the need to deal with the capital expense of buying hardware VPN appliances, or the operational complexity of scaling and patching. Customers can choose certificate-based or Active Directory authentication, and benefit from tighter security controls by defining access control rules based on Active Directory groups. Using a single console, you can easily monitor and manage all of your VPN connections. AWS Client VPN allows you to choose from OpenVPN-based clients, giving your employees the option to use the device of their choice, including Windows, Mac, iOS, Android and Linux.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, see the AWS VPN product \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/vpn/\"\u003epage\u003c/a\u003e, as well as the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/what-is.html\"\u003eadministrator\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-user/user-getting-started.html\"\u003euser\u003c/a\u003e documentation.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:00:52Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/05/aws-client-vpn-now-available-in-asia-pacific-mumbai-and-asia-pacific-tokyo-aws-regions/","postDateTime":"2019-05-20T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Client VPN Now Available in Asia Pacific (Mumbai) and Asia Pacific (Tokyo) AWS Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN is now available in the Asia Pacific (Mumbai) and Asia Pacific (Tokyo) AWS Regions. AWS Client VPN is already available in US East (Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon),\u0026nbsp;EU (Frankfurt), EU (Ireland),\u0026nbsp;EU (London),\u0026nbsp;Asia Pacific (Singapore), and Asia Pacific (Sydney) AWS Regions. Support for other AWS Regions is coming soon.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-04-aws-client-vpn-is-now-available-in-four-additional-aws-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/04/aws-client-vpn-is-now-available-in-four-additional-aws-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:11:28+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:25:54+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN is now available in the EU (Frankfurt), EU (London), Asia  Pacific (Singapore), and Asia Pacific (Sydney) AWS Regions. AWS Client  VPN was already available in US East (Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West  (Oregon), and EU (Ireland) AWS Regions. Support for other AWS Regions  is coming soon.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN provides you with the ability to securely access your AWS and on-premises networks from anywhere, using OpenVPN-based clients.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEmployees often need to access company resources while off premises, such as at home or on the road. Until today, to enable access, you could run a hardware VPN appliance in your data center or deploy a software-based VPN appliance on Amazon EC2. Setup, security, and maintenance of self-managed client-based VPN solutions present an operational challenge and ongoing burden. Unforeseen events, such as a snow day, could require a large number of employees to connect from a remote location and further strain your VPN. It often led to reduced VPN availability for employees.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith AWS Client VPN, you can now provide highly available and secure VPN access to all your employees regardless of their location. AWS Client VPN is a pay-as-you-go fully-managed service, eliminating the need to deal with the capital expense of buying hardware VPN appliances, or the operational complexity of scaling and patching. Customers can choose certificate-based or Active Directory authentication, and benefit from tighter security controls by defining access control rules based on Active Directory groups. Using a single console, you can easily monitor and manage all of your VPN connections. AWS Client VPN allows you to choose from OpenVPN-based clients, giving your employees the option to use the device of their choice, including Windows, Mac, iOS, Android and Linux.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, see the AWS VPN \u003ca href\u003d\"http://aws.amazon.com/vpn\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e, as well as the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/what-is.html\"\u003eadministrator\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-user/user-getting-started.html\"\u003euser\u003c/a\u003e documentation.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:00:13Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/04/aws-client-vpn-is-now-available-in-four-additional-aws-regions/","postDateTime":"2019-04-16T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Client VPN is Now Available in Four Additional AWS Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Client VPN is now available in the EU (Frankfurt), EU (London), Asia  Pacific (Singapore), and Asia Pacific (Sydney) AWS Regions. AWS Client  VPN was already available in US East (Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West  (Oregon), and EU (Ireland) AWS Regions. Support for other AWS Regions  is coming soon.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-client-vpn","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-client-vpn","description":"general:products/aws-client-vpn","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:39+0000"}]}],"metadata":{"count":33,"totalHits":33},"fieldTypes":{"regionalAvailability":"LongText","nofollow":"Boolean","date":"Date","language":"Text","title":"Text","postDateTime":"DateTime","body":"Text","postSummary":"LongText","ctaLabel":"Text","mediaThumbnail":"Text","nosnippet":"Boolean","price":"Text","ctaLink":"URL","headline":"Text","contentType":"Text","bodyBack":"LongText","secondaryCTALabel":"Text","primaryCTALink":"URL","noindex":"Boolean","level":"Text","heading":"Text","mediaType":"Text","mediaAlt":"Text","headlineUrl":"Text","mediaSrc":"URL","durationMinutes":"Number","badge":"JSON","videoImageUrl":"URL","postBody":"LongText","secondaryCTALink":"URL","Video":"URL","modifiedDate":"DateTime","namePerson":"Text","location":"Text","time":"Text","publishedDate":"DateTime","durationReadtime":"Number","primaryCTALabel":"Text"}}